# Reflection - Unit 4: Navigation and App Architecture

## What I Learned
- How to explain activities and their lifecycles.
- The basics of modern Android architecture using ViewModels and StateFlow.
- How navigation works between multiple screens.
- Principles of adaptive and responsive design for different screen sizes.

## Challenges
- Understanding StateFlow and UDF patterns required careful study.
- Simulating navigation outside Android Studio was limited.
- Responsive design concepts were new and required practice.

## My Choices
- I used Kotlin-only simulations to practice architecture and navigation logic.
- I represented adaptive UI with simple console outputs for different screen sizes.
- I focused on clean, modular code to reflect architecture principles.

## Outcome
Unit 4 helped me connect Kotlin logic with Android architecture concepts.  
I practiced ViewModel, state management, navigation, and responsive design, preparing me for full Android app development projects.
